==English==
{{wp|Text messaging}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-text message.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[brief]] [[electronic]] message sent between [[mobile phone]]s.
#: {{syn|en|text}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian
|date=December 14, 2011
|author=Steven Morris
|title=Devon woman jailed for 168 days for killing kitten in microwave
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2011/dec/14/woman-killed-kitten-microwave-jail
|passage=After the kitten had died, Robins sent a '''text message''' to Knutton saying: "Remember the saying: 'What goes around comes around?' It has started already to bite you in the arse. The cat? Karma."|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261013161452/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2011/dec/14/woman-killed-kitten-microwave-jail|archivedate=13 October 2026}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|title=An internet of airborne things|date=2012-12-01|volume=405|issue=8813|page=3 (Technology Quarterly)|url=http://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21567193-networking-enthusiasts-dream-building-drone-powered-internet-carry-objects
|passage=A farmer could place an order for a new tractor part by '''text message''' and pay for it by mobile money-transfer. A supplier many miles away would then take the part to the local matternet station for airborne dispatch via drone.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201062641/https://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21567193-networking-enthusiasts-dream-building-drone-powered-internet-carry-objects|archivedate=1 December 2017}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2018|author=James Lambert|title=A multitude of ‘lishes’: The nomenclature of hybridity|journal=English World-Wide|page=10|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318367113_A_multitude_of_lishes_The_nomenclature_of_hybridity
|text=Similarly, ''Fingilish'' usually refers to transliterated Farsi in chatrooms, '''text messages''', and the like.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260210120000/https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318367113_A_multitude_of_lishes_The_nomenclature_of_hybridity|archivedate=10 February 2026}}

